# {{source}}, a Docket source

Reads {{source}} with the user's own tools and hands what they returned to Docket untouched; `mapper.py` next to
this file turns a run's captures into records. `docket source new` wrote this folder from Docket's blank template:
fill in each section below, then the mapping in `mapper.py`. Docket's Plaud reference shows a whole source:
https://github.com/serionist/docket/tree/main/examples/sources/plaud

Claude Code doesn't load this file as a skill from `.claude/skills/sources/{{source}}/`: whatever runs the source
reads it by its path.

## What it reads

Which tools read {{source}} (an MCP server, a plugin, the browser), and which of them return its content. The ones the
capture hook posts are listed in `vault.yaml` under `sources.{{source}}.tools`, by their own names, without the
host's `mcp__` prefix.

## A run

The capture hook posts each tool's result as it came; Claude never retypes a payload. The run's manifest counts the
captures, and Docket maps them when the manifest closes the run.

| Step | What |
|---|---|
| Sign in | what "not signed in" looks like, and the way back in |
| Skip | the held ids, and what raw and staging already hold, read through the service; skip those, to save calls |
| List | newest first, without date filters, until a page's oldest item is before the window's start |
| Each item | the calls that fetch it whole |
| Rate limits | what a limit looks like; pause and retry with growing pauses; still limited, end the run, and the kept window resumes it |
| Waiting | what the mapper reports as waiting, and when it is asked for again |

Recordings and mail fetched before Docket go in with `docket ingest {{source}} <folder> --vault <vault>`, through the
same mapper.

## What it makes

| Record | rid | When |
|---|---|---|
| each item | `{{source}}:<its own id>` | what makes it complete |

A held item is skipped before anything of it is parsed, and nothing the mapper reports carries a title.

## Changing the mapper

Every record the lookback reads again gets a new version when the mapper's output changes, and the gate asks about it
again.

- Keep the output stable: change it only for a real change in what {{source}} says.
- Pin golden versions in the tests, as the Plaud reference does, so a change shows before it runs.
- Pull the project on every machine before its next sync, so two machines never map one item two ways.
